  "question": {
    "text": "Let the normals at all the points on a given curve pass through a fixed point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the curve passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>, given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>All normals of circle passes through centre</p><p>Radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0122_a3219e85066b.png\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 170px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p>"
